WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.089 --> 00:00:04.330
If you want to hear all three of my theories
about Hospice, then stick around to the end

00:00:04.330 --> 00:00:05.410
of this video.

00:00:05.410 --> 00:00:06.680
Sponsored by Crypt TV.

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:15.300
Crypt TV has just brought back Hospice, the
hospital ghost story that originally haunted

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:18.010
doctors and patients in late 2017.

00:00:18.010 --> 00:00:21.700
So before we explore the Things You Missed
in the latest episode, let’s revisit what

00:00:21.700 --> 00:00:23.520
happened back in episode one.

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:28.240
Sharon is a nurse taking care of a patient
named Mr. Nowak, who suddenly sits up and

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.570
starts suffocating.

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:33.520
Next thing we know, his corpse is being taken
away, and Sharon is pretty shaken up by the

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:34.520
incident.

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:37.750
The doctor gives her the option to leave,
but she decides to still work her night shift.

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:42.079
As the body is taken away, a marble falls
off the stretcher, and Sharon holds onto it.

00:00:42.079 --> 00:00:45.970
Later that night, one of her co-workers, Jake,
asks Sharon to cover for him as he takes off

00:00:45.970 --> 00:00:48.680
30 minutes early, leaving Sharon alone in
the hospice wing.

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:52.149
Shortly after, the lights start flickering
before Sharon is attacked by the ghost of

00:00:52.149 --> 00:00:54.900
Mr. Nowak, who cannot be seen on the security
camera footage.

00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:59.079
When the doctor eventually finds her body,
he doesn’t seem as shocked as he should

00:00:59.079 --> 00:01:00.079
be.

00:01:00.079 --> 00:01:01.079
“Not again.”

00:01:01.079 --> 00:01:04.400
So episode 2 starts with a new nurse named
Alice Carroll.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:08.030
She’s having some kind of vision of a kid
being attacked by a monster -- we can tell

00:01:08.030 --> 00:01:11.740
from the symbol on it’s head and the fangs,
that this is Brute, from the Crypt Monster

00:01:11.740 --> 00:01:15.469
Universe episode The Door In The Woods which
is about four kids who accidentally unleash

00:01:15.469 --> 00:01:17.380
this monster upon their colony.

00:01:22.340 --> 00:01:25.320
Alice is pulled out of her vision by the sound
of flatlining.

00:01:25.329 --> 00:01:26.899
She reports on the time of death 11:05.

00:01:26.899 --> 00:01:31.210
This doesn’t match up with the time we just
saw on the EKG machine, which could either

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:34.490
mean that this is still part of the vision
of the kid being mauled by Brute, or this

00:01:34.490 --> 00:01:38.250
is just a small continuity error, because
the date also doesn’t match the date put

00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.909
on the patient’s morgue tag either.

00:01:39.909 --> 00:01:44.229
The doctor notices she is distressed and tells
her, “you’ll get used to them… the dead.”

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:48.710
At first, he seems to be referring to her
getting used to patients dying, but on closer

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:52.369
inspection, he could also be referring to
the ghosts seen in the hospice ward.

00:01:52.369 --> 00:01:56.599
Alice offers to wheel the patient down to
the morgue, so her fellow nurse Barbara Hasley

00:01:56.599 --> 00:02:00.329
gives her the instructions to take a right
at the end of the basement corridor, emphasizing

00:02:00.329 --> 00:02:01.739
to ONLY go right.

00:02:01.739 --> 00:02:06.489
Alice’s curiosity leads her to go left anyway
after seeing the sign that it leads to hospice

00:02:06.489 --> 00:02:09.160
wing, but she gets caught pretty quickly.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:14.099
“That wing is closed.”

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:16.560
It is?

00:02:16.569 --> 00:02:19.430
Then why is the door open with the lights
on?

00:02:19.430 --> 00:02:23.340
Is there some presence trying to beckon Alice
into this forbidden territory?

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:28.540
When Alice gets into the morgue, she startles
the metalhead coroner, who’s cleaning up

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:30.100
blood at the time of her arrival.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:34.849
Alice notices a mortuary cabinet labeled with
the name Kane and asks if this is Dr. Kane’s

00:02:34.849 --> 00:02:37.750
son, probably the same Dr. Kane who owns this
hospital.

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:41.819
Dan tells her that the kid died of heart disease,
which doesn’t match up with the visions

00:02:41.819 --> 00:02:45.200
or the fact that he’s cleaning up blood
off the table when she arrives, though the

00:02:45.200 --> 00:02:48.080
blood theoretically could have been from one
of the others.

00:02:48.080 --> 00:02:52.180
Alice goes to investigate more about Norman
Kane, but before she gets the chance, Barbara

00:02:52.180 --> 00:02:55.489
shows up and warns her again to stay out of
the hospice wing.

00:02:55.489 --> 00:02:59.959
Back in the morgue, Kane’s cabinet bursts
open and this monster emerges and throws Dan

00:02:59.959 --> 00:03:03.590
into a transformer box, causing lights to
flicker around the hospital.

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:06.569
I like how there’s actually a practical
reason for the lights flickering, and it’s

00:03:06.569 --> 00:03:09.430
not just explained away by the hospital being
haunted.

00:03:09.430 --> 00:03:12.700
This also ties back into the flickering lights
from the first episode and that leads me to

00:03:12.700 --> 00:03:16.060
my first theory: episode 1 takes place after
the rest of this season.

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:19.840
This can be supported by the flickering lights
that were never fully fixed after episode

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:23.599
2, and the fact that the doctor says, “not
again” after discovering Sharon’s body

00:03:23.599 --> 00:03:24.599
in the first one.

00:03:24.599 --> 00:03:28.150
The date on the security footage from the
first episode is November 10th, just 8 days

00:03:28.150 --> 00:03:30.970
after the death of Mr. Conley in the first
episode.

00:03:30.970 --> 00:03:33.829
My second theory is that Alice has psychic
abilities.

00:03:33.829 --> 00:03:37.209
Upon arriving at the hospital for her first
day, she’s able to see a vision of Kane’s

00:03:37.209 --> 00:03:41.940
son being killed, and she’s even seen rubbing
her head as if focusing some kind of psychic

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:42.940
energy.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:45.620
When she goes down to the basement corridor,
she takes the left into the hospice wing,

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:47.680
despite just being told to go right.

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:51.790
I feel like something from beyond lured her
to go explore in that direction.

00:03:51.790 --> 00:03:54.900
She also seems pretty quick to believe in
the supernatural when her and Barbara discuss

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:56.129
it.

00:03:56.129 --> 00:03:58.920
“Do yourself a favor.

00:03:58.920 --> 00:04:00.540
Forget what you heard.”

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:01.120
“Why?

00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:03.499
Are the stories real?”

00:04:03.499 --> 00:04:06.939
Then towards the end of the episode she goes
back to explore the area again, and it looks

00:04:06.939 --> 00:04:10.909
as if she sees something at the end of the
hall, but when we cut to the reverse, there’s

00:04:10.909 --> 00:04:11.909
nothing there.

00:04:11.909 --> 00:04:15.890
The second theory leads into my third and
final theory: Alice’s co-worker Barbara

00:04:15.890 --> 00:04:18.500
is one of the ghosts, trying to lure Alice
in.

00:04:18.500 --> 00:04:21.700
If Alice is a psychic, she’d be the only
one who sees Barbara.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:25.470
There’s no interaction between Dr. Evans
and Barbara in the opening scene...

00:04:25.470 --> 00:04:30.229
“Five years I’m here and he hasn’t looked
at me once.”

00:04:30.229 --> 00:04:34.090
Barbara also gives oddly specific directions
for Alice to only turn right at the end of

00:04:34.090 --> 00:04:37.840
the basement corridor, it’s almost as if
she wants to pique Alice’s curiosity and

00:04:37.840 --> 00:04:39.610
lure her into the haunted wing.

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:43.250
The other scene with Barbara is again just
the two of them, and again, Barbara doesn’t

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:46.740
provide specific details about why Alice should
keep out of the hospice wing.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:50.660
If you have any theories about Hospice and
how it ties into the other Crypt series, be

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:53.199
sure to let me know in the comments.

00:04:53.199 --> 00:04:56.940
And if you haven’t already, make sure you’re
subscribed to Crypt TV for new scary videos

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:59.300
every Monday, Wednesday and Friday.

00:04:59.300 --> 00:05:02.870
Every Friday they upload a new chapter to
